From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 14:01:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ether: QS tile layout and RobinLed listener access

Two device-level resource overlays:

- `quick_settings_tiles_default` adds the NFC and LiveDisplay tiles to the default Quick Settings
  layout. Both features default OFF, so the tiles put each one tap away. Only consulted when there is
  no stored QS layout, i.e. on a fresh install.
- `config_defaultListenerAccessPackages` auto-grants notification-listener access to
  com.nextbit.robinled, so the rear LEDs work without the user enabling it by hand.

The theme default is not set here: the forge's dark-default option sets config_defaultNightMode in
frameworks/base, and a device overlay would silently override it.

The accent is no longer set here. It used to be seven `*_device_default_*` colours in a framework-res
overlay, which is the pre-Monet mechanism; on Android 12 and newer the dynamic-colour palette governs
those surfaces. The forge's teal-skin option seeds the same #009D94 as a Monet preset with
color_source=preset, so it survives wallpaper changes, and it is the same mechanism every other
device here uses.

The DeskClock `widget_max_clock_font_size` override is dropped as dead. It sizes the home-screen
clock widget, and no preset has one: minimal-home strips every appwidget from the default workspace,
and on a GApps build GoogleClock overrides DeskClock so the overlay is not compiled in at all.
---
 .../base/core/res/res/values/config.xml       |  5 ++++
 .../packages/SystemUI/res/values/config.xml   | 29 ++++---------------
 2 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 23 deletions(-)

diff --git a/overlay/frameworks/base/core/res/res/values/config.xml b/overlay/frameworks/base/core/res/res/values/config.xml
index d35c036..b58855e 100644
--- a/overlay/frameworks/base/core/res/res/values/config.xml
+++ b/overlay/frameworks/base/core/res/res/values/config.xml
@@ -276,4 +276,9 @@
     <!-- AOSP WFD -->
     <bool name="config_enableWifiDisplay">true</bool>
 
+    <!-- Auto-grant notification-listener access to RobinLed so it can drive the rear LEDs
+         without the user enabling it manually. NotificationManagerService reads this as a
+         colon-separated *string*; a string-array is silently ignored. -->
+    <string name="config_defaultListenerAccessPackages" translatable="false">com.nextbit.robinled</string>
+
 </resources>
diff --git a/overlay/frameworks/base/packages/SystemUI/res/values/config.xml b/overlay/frameworks/base/packages/SystemUI/res/values/config.xml
index 74df52f..b3f3dcb 100644
--- a/overlay/frameworks/base/packages/SystemUI/res/values/config.xml
+++ b/overlay/frameworks/base/packages/SystemUI/res/values/config.xml
@@ -1,26 +1,9 @@
